{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH3GramNondegeneracy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeH3GramNondegeneracy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTraceOnHecke","lean:module:QOU.Shared.DetFin","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.NonsingularInverse","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.gramMatrix_det_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.gramMatrix_det_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3GramNondegeneracy.lean#L152-L205","doc":"**Nondegeneracy at the Hecke specialization** `h = q - q⁻¹`: the Gram\ndeterminant is nonzero away from the four degeneracy points.\n\n* **Quintic factor**, via `z² - hz - 1 = (z - q)(z + q⁻¹)`: the eigenvalue\n  channels `z = q` and `z = -q⁻¹`.  Each is a **corank-5** collapse — the Gram\n  drops to rank 1 there, not to rank 5.\n* **Quadratic factor**, via\n  `q³·((h²+4)z² - (h³+4h)z - 1) = ((q²+1)z - q³)((q³+q)z + 1)`: the Markov-weight\n  zeros `z = q³/(q²+1)` and `z = -1/(q(q²+1))`.  Each is a **corank-1** collapse,\n  and the block that drops out is **one-dimensional** in both cases:\n  the sign representation `(1³)` at `z = q³/(q²+1)`, whose radical is the\n  q-antisymmetriser `(-q³, q², q², -q, -q, 1)`, and the trivial representation\n  `(3)` at `z = -1/(q(q²+1))`, whose radical is the q-symmetriser.\n\n  This corrects an earlier reading of these two as `(2,1)`-block zeros.  `(2,1)`\n  has dimension 2, and a block of dimension `d` leaving the trace costs the Gram\n  `d²` dimensions — so `(2,1)` would give corank 4, where the measured corank is\n  1.  The statement below is unaffected: all four hypotheses are exactly the\n  vanishing locus and the proof never used the attribution.\n\n  The `z = q³/(q²+1)` case is convention D, canonical since the owner ruling of\n  2026-08-15, so this is the identity behind\n  `QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic.gramMatrixD_det_eq_zero`; its\n  `gramRadicalD` is the same vector, reached independently.  Reading it as `(1³)`\n  rather than `(2,1)` is what connects it to `y_λ = 0` for partitions with `≥ 3`\n  rows (bean `qou-8iru`) — the same degeneracy seen from the weights.\n\n  Corank and block identification measured exactly over `ℚ(q)` in\n  `computations/probes/h3_gram_degeneracy_block_identification_probe.py`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.exists_pairing_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.exists_pairing_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3GramNondegeneracy.lean#L120-L150","doc":"**Trace nondegeneracy from the determinant** — the Wenzl-hypothesis\nrealization at rank 3: whenever `det G ≠ 0`, every nonzero `y ∈ H₃(q)` pairs\nnontrivially with some `w` under the Markov trace.  This exact shape is the\n`semisimple_ascend` trace-nondegeneracy hypothesis of\n`QOU.Machinery.HeckeTower.WenzlTowerStep`, here discharged concretely for the\nexplicit H₃ trace.  The witness is a basis vector: pick `j` with\n`(y ᵥ* G) j ≠ 0` (possible since `G` is invertible) and take\n`w = Pi.single j 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.gramMatrix_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.gramMatrix_det","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3GramNondegeneracy.lean#L106-L118","doc":"**Closed-form determinant** of the H₃ Markov-trace Gram matrix:\n`det G = -(z² - hz - 1)⁵ · ((h²+4)z² - (h³+4h)z - 1)`.\nMatches `detG_zh` of the sympy witness\n`computations/h3_gram/hecke-h3-markov-gram.data.json` (numerically\ncross-checked, e.g. both sides `= -736` at `z = 3, h = 2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.trM_mulNF_eq_dotProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.trM_mulNF_eq_dotProduct","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3GramNondegeneracy.lean#L94-L102","doc":"**Bilinearity in matrix form**: the trace pairing of arbitrary elements is\nthe Gram bilinear form, `tr_M(u · v) = ∑ⱼ (∑ᵢ uᵢ Gᵢⱼ) vⱼ` — the plain-sum\n(`vecMul`-free) phrasing of `tr_M(u·v) = (u ᵥ* G) ⬝ᵥ v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.gramMatrix_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.gramMatrix_eq","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3GramNondegeneracy.lean#L85-L92","doc":"`gramMatrix` **is** the Gram matrix of the Markov-trace pairing: entry\n`(i, j)` is `tr_M(bᵢ · bⱼ)` for the basis vectors `bᵢ = Pi.single i 1`.\nRe-derives every entry of the sympy table from the `trM`/`mulNF` substrate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H3.gramMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H3.gramMatrix","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH3GramNondegeneracy.lean#L60-L82","doc":"The **Gram matrix** of the H₃(q) Markov-trace pairing\n`⟨bᵢ, bⱼ⟩ = tr_M(bᵢ · bⱼ)` on the GB normal-form basis\n`[γ, σ₀, σ₁, L₊, L₋, e⁻]`.  Entries are the polynomial-expanded forms of\n`computations/h3_gram/hecke-h3-markov-gram.data.json` (`gram` field); the\nidentification with the trace pairing is `gramMatrix_eq`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}